,float,"• Data Type: The course discusses the ‘float’ data type in programming.
• Usage: ‘Float’ is used for variables that will store floating-point values, also known as real numbers.
• Memory: Floating points values always take up 4 bytes of memory (32 bits).
• Precision: The precision of a float is limited due to its 32-bit structure. Some of these bits might be used for an integer part, limiting how precise we can be.",
